SURG = ("Describe radiofrequency/ electrosurgery modalities used for benign lesions.", ["Electrodesiccation (monoterminal, superficial dehydration), electrofulguration (sparking, no contact), electrocoagulation (biterminal, deeper), electrosection (cutting — radiofrequency 'radiosurgery' 3–4 MHz gives fine cuts with less thermal damage); precautions — pacemakers (use bipolar), alcohol-based prep (fire), smoke plume (HPV), avoid on keloid-prone skin"])
CRYO = ("Explain the principles of cryotherapy (PYQ).", ["Liquid nitrogen (−196 °C): rapid freezing causes intracellular ice crystals, cell dehydration, vascular stasis and ischaemic necrosis; slow thaw maximises damage; techniques — spray, cotton-tipped applicator, cryoprobe; lethal temperature for benign lesions −20 to −30 °C, malignant −50 °C (double freeze–thaw)", "Side effects: pain, blistering, hypo/ hyperpigmentation (avoid in dark skin cosmetic areas), scarring, nerve damage over superficial nerves, alopecia"])
